7. Final Result
The mathematical analysis shows that Linear Search requires a number of comparisons proportional to the input size. Recursive Binary Search reduces the search area by half in each step, resulting in logarithmic search time. Hash Table Search provides approximately constant average search time after preprocessing, provided collisions are limited.

